# GCE Training Operations

## Instance + Infra

- GCE instance: `isaacsim`, zone: `us-central1-a`, project: `gg-swarm`
- Repo path on VM: `~/ggSwarm`
- GCS bucket: `gs://gg-swarm-training-logs`  ← ONLY valid bucket; never use gs://gg-swarm/results
- SSH prefix for all remote commands: `gcloud compute ssh isaacsim --zone=us-central1-a --command="..."`

## CRITICAL: Env Var Must Be Inlined

`source ~/.bashrc` does NOT propagate to backgrounded subprocesses over SSH.
Always inline `GGSWARM_GCS_URI` directly in the nohup call:

```bash
# WRONG — env var not visible to backgrounded process
source ~/.bashrc && nohup bash scripts/cloud/train_and_push.sh ... &

# CORRECT — inlined before nohup
GGSWARM_GCS_URI=gs://gg-swarm-training-logs nohup bash scripts/cloud/train_and_push.sh ... &
```

## Deploy + Launch Training (Remote)

**Windows (PowerShell, repo root):** one command does `git push`, VM `git pull`, and detached `train_and_push.sh` (GCS URI inlined on the remote):

```powershell
.\scripts\cloud\gce_train_launch.ps1
```

Defaults: `hover-stability train --headless --max_iterations 80000`. Pass training args after the script name (and optional `-SkipGitPush`). Git branch defaults to `main`; override with `$env:GGSWARM_GIT_BRANCH` if needed. Skip push if you already pushed:

```powershell
.\scripts\cloud\gce_train_launch.ps1 hover-stability train --headless --max_iterations 92000
.\scripts\cloud\gce_train_launch.ps1 -SkipGitPush phase2 train --headless --max_iterations 120000
```

```bash
# 1. Push local code changes
git push origin main

# 2. Pull on VM
gcloud compute ssh isaacsim --zone=us-central1-a --command="cd ~/ggSwarm && git pull origin main"

# 3. Launch training — unique timestamped log file each run
gcloud compute ssh isaacsim --zone=us-central1-a --command="cd ~/ggSwarm && GGSWARM_GCS_URI=gs://gg-swarm-training-logs nohup bash scripts/cloud/train_and_push.sh phase2 train --headless --max_iterations 120000 > ~/train_phase2_\$(date +%Y%m%d_%H%M%S).log 2>&1 &"
```

## Kill Training

```bash
# Find training PID
gcloud compute ssh isaacsim --zone=us-central1-a --command="ps aux | grep 'python scripts' | grep -v grep"

# Graceful kill — triggers GCS push via trap in train_and_push.sh
gcloud compute ssh isaacsim --zone=us-central1-a --command="kill -SIGTERM <PID>"

# Nuclear — kills ALL python processes (use only if graceful fails)
gcloud compute ssh isaacsim --zone=us-central1-a --command="killall -9 python3 python 2>/dev/null"
```

## Monitor Training

```bash
# Live tail (blocking)
gcloud compute ssh isaacsim --zone=us-central1-a --command="tail -f ~/train_phase2_<timestamp>.log"

# Latest PROGRESS line only (non-blocking)
gcloud compute ssh isaacsim --zone=us-central1-a --command="grep '\[PROGRESS\]' ~/train_phase2_<timestamp>.log | tail -3"
```

[PROGRESS] format (after ETA fix): `N/120,000 (X.X%) | iters_per_sec=16.7 | eta=HH:MM:SS`
ETA is based on max_iterations (120k), not total_timesteps (7.68M).

## Sync Results (GCS → Local)

```bash
# List available runs in GCS
python scripts/cloud/list_checkpoints.py --family marl

# Pull latest run to local logs/
python scripts/cloud/pull_results_from_gcs.py --family marl --latest 1

# Preview without downloading
python scripts/cloud/pull_results_from_gcs.py --dry-run
```

Results land in: `logs/skrl/ggswarm_marl/<timestamp>_mappo_torch/`

## Local Commands (after sync)

```bash
python scripts/run.py phase2 eval --num_episodes 5 --checkpoint "logs/skrl/ggswarm_marl/<run>/checkpoints/best_agent.pt"
python scripts/run.py phase2 play --checkpoint "logs/skrl/ggswarm_marl/<run>/checkpoints/best_agent.pt"
tensorboard --logdir logs/skrl/ggswarm_marl
```

## MANDATORY: GCE is for Training Only

**ALL** of the following must run on the **LOCAL Windows machine**, NOT on GCE:

- `phase2 eval` / `phase3 eval` / `hover-stability eval` (eval scripts require Isaac Lab locally)
- `phase2 play` / `phase3 play` (playback)
- `phase2 assess` / `hover-stability assess` (post-training scorecard)
- `tensorboard` monitoring
- `list_checkpoints.py`, `pull_results_from_gcs.py`
- `analyze_checkpoints.py`, `check_convergence.py`
- Any `git` operations

The GCE `isaacsim` instance is ONLY used for:

- `phase2 train` / `phase3 train` / `hover-stability train` via `train_and_push.sh`
- Nothing else

Do **NOT** suggest running eval, play, assess, or analysis scripts via `gcloud compute ssh --command`.
After training completes: SIGTERM → confirm GCS push → pull locally → eval locally.

